  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRA_06_02_Urban Livelihoods _supplementary grant to programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This approval is a supplement to the EC funded Urban Community Development programme (BRA0602) which aims to improve the quality of housing and basic services for low-income families, (in particular female and youth headed households) living in the shanty towns and tenement blocks of Sao Paulo, Brazil&#x2019;s largest city.   
To do this, it will use three strategies: advocacy, campaigning and capacity building at the grassroots. The three programmatic lines of the programme are as follows:
a)	Guarantee urban public policy for housing that will benefit low income families. This will be done through the monitoring of public housing policy and programmes, raising awareness of the situation of low income populations in Sao Paulo and strengthening local community networks, as well as civil society networks at the national and international level. 
b)	Increase the participation of women and young people( who live in the Favelas and poor areas of the city) in community groups and in spaces of consultation and decision making forums on urban issues ( associations etc).
c)	Increase the capacity and impact of local organisations in the defence of the right to housing. This includes training the 3 partner organisations in various areas, such as financial management and programme planning and monitoring, so that they are better able to carry out their work, increase their impact and promote a more democratic, just and participatory city.

The programme budget is restrictive and inflexible and some core costs were not included at the outset. This specific approval is a  one off grant to supplement the programme in order to cover the following:

1)	Deficit in funding the salaries of the EC project staff- MDF.  (30000GBP)- 10000GBP from BSCG budget and 20000GBP from the approval of the bid for ID savings.
2)	Cost of accountants for each of the three partners MDF, CCJ, APOIO (previously allocated to BRA499- Audit fund but now being approved here) 11627.11GBP
3)	Costs of deficit in resources available for rent of APOIO building ( amount included in EC project does now not cover full rent amount)- 5790.34GBP</narrative>
  </description>
